/repair of bad cells - local refinement/coarsening hooks optional Quality metrics to compute: - cell volume - minimum/maximum face area - non-orthogonality - skewness - aspect ratio / elongation - face warpage - pyramid volume positivity - boundary face validity Default acceptance thresholds: - min cell volume > 1e-30 - max nonOrthogonality < 70 warning, < 85 error - max skewness < 4 warning, < 10 error - no negative volumes - no non-manifold topology - all boundary faces owned by exactly one cell ## 10. Export Support: - OpenFOAM polyMesh export - VTK export - JSON quality/report export OpenFOAM export requirements: - write points, faces, owner, neighbour, boundary - correct face orientation - valid boundary patches - loadable by ParaView and OpenFOAM utilities - if OpenFOAM is available, run `checkMesh` as validation # DATA MODEL Design a clean mesh data structure. Minimum required entities: - points - faces as vertex loops - cells as face lists - boundary patches - feature edges - size field samples - quality report Preferred architecture: - explicit topology with owner/neighbour for volume cells - support arbitrary polygonal faces - support arbitrary polyhedral cells - safe topological edits - validation functions # PUBLIC API Expose a stable high-level API similar to: namespace autopoly { struct Vec3 { double x, y, z; }; struct BoundingBox { Vec3 min; Vec3 max; }; struct GeometryOptions { double mergeTolerance = 1e-9; bool fillSmallHoles = true; double maxHoleArea = -1.0; bool orientNormals = true; bool repairSelfIntersections = false; }; struct FeatureOptions { bool enable = true; double featureAngleDeg = 30.0; double curvatureSensitivity = 0.5; }; struct SizeFieldOptions { double globalSize = 0.05; double minSize = 0.001; double maxSize = 1.0; double curvatureAdaptivity = 0.5; double proximityAdaptivity = 0.5; double maxGrowthRate = 1.2; }; struct SurfaceMeshOptions { double targetSize = 0.03; double minQuality = 0.2; int maxIterations = 20; bool preserveFeatures = true; }; struct VolumeMeshOptions { int seed = 12345; int lloydIterations = 30; double boundaryConformity = 0.9; bool mergeCoplanarFaces = true; double coplanarAngleToleranceDeg = 1.0; double smallFaceAreaTolerance = 1e-12; double minCellVolume = 1e-30; }; struct BoundaryLayerOptions { bool enable = false; int layers = 3; double firstHeight = 0.0005; double growthRate = 1.2; double maxThickness = 0.01; bool smoothNormals = true; bool detectCollisions = true; }; struct QualityOptions { double maxNonOrthoWarn = 70.0; double maxNonOrthoFail = 85.0; double maxSkewnessWarn = 4.0; double maxSkewnessFail = 10.0; double maxAspectRatioWarn = 100.0; double maxAspectRatioFail = 1000.0; }; struct ExportOptions { bool writeVtk = true; bool writeOpenFoam = true; bool writeJsonReport = true; std::string outputDirectory = \"output\"; }; struct ProgressInfo { int stagePercent = 0; std::string stageName; std::string message; bool cancellable = true; }; using ProgressCallback = std::function<void(const ProgressInfo&)>; using CancelToken = std::function<bool()>; struct MeshingParameters { GeometryOptions geometry; FeatureOptions features; SizeFieldOptions sizeField; SurfaceMeshOptions surface; VolumeMeshOptions volume; BoundaryLayerOptions boundaryLayer; QualityOptions quality; ExportOptions exportOptions; }; struct MeshingResult { bool success = false; std::string message; std::string outputDirectory; size_t pointCount = 0; size_t cellCount = 0; size_t faceCount = 0; size_t boundaryPatchCount = 0; double minVolume = 0.0; double maxNonOrthogonality = 0.0; double maxSkewness = 0.0; double maxAspectRatio = 0.0; std::vector<std::string> warnings; std::vector<std::string> errors; }; class Mesher { public: virtual ~Mesher() = default; virtual MeshingResult run( const std::filesystem::path& inputGeometry, const MeshingParameters& params, ProgressCallback progress = {}, CancelToken cancel = {}) = 0; }; std::unique_ptr<Mesher> createMesher(); } // namespace autopoly # GUI INTEGRATION REQUIREMENTS The library must be GUI-friendly. Provide: - progress callbacks by stage - cancellation support - parameter validation - JSON parameter schema - intermediate preview outputs if possible - thread-safe usage guidance - clear error/warning reporting Suggested stages: 1. load geometry 2. repair geometry 3. extract features 4. build size field 5. surface remesh 6. generate seeds 7. CVT / Voronoi 8. boundary clip 9. boundary layer 10. optimization 11. quality check 12. export # ALGORITHMIC EXPECTATIONS Use robust methods, not brittle heuristics. Recommended core approach: 1. Build a watertight, oriented, feature-aware surface mesh. 2. Build an AABB tree and signed distance field / inside-outside oracle. 3. Generate adaptive seeds using the size field. 4. Compute constrained CVT via Lloyd iterations. 5. Build Voronoi cells as half-space intersections. 6. Clip cells against the domain boundary. 7. Extract boundary faces from clipped cells. 8. Snap/project boundary entities to CAD/surface. 9. Merge coplanar faces and simplify small topological artifacts. 10. Optionally extrude boundary layers. 11. Optimize and validate topology/quality. 12. Export. If you choose a different robust approach, justify it and prove it with tests. # PROJECT STRUCTURE Create a clean repository layout: autopoly/ CMakeLists.txt README.md docs/ architecture.md parameters.md validation.md include/autopoly/ Types.h Geometry.h Feature.h SizeField.h SurfaceMesher.h VolumeMesher.h BoundaryLayer.h Quality.h Exporter.h Mesher.h Factory.h src/ Geometry.cpp Feature.cpp SizeField.cpp SurfaceMesher.cpp VolumeMesher.cpp BoundaryLayer.cpp Quality.cpp Exporter.cpp Mesher.cpp Factory.cpp cgal/ CgalKernel.h CgalKernel.cpp apps/ autopoly_cli.cpp python/ autopoly_pybind.cpp tests/ test_geometry.cpp test_surface_mesher.cpp test_volume_mesher.cpp test_quality.cpp test_export.cpp data/ cube.stl sphere.stl cylinder.stl broken_cube.stl thin_gap.stl sharp_feature.stl # TESTING REQUIREMENTS Add automated tests for: ## Unit tests, max no-progress 3"}
