QUIREMENTS The library must be GUI-friendly. Provide: - progress callbacks by stage - cancellation support - parameter validation - JSON parameter schema - intermediate preview outputs if possible - thread-safe usage guidance - clear error/warning reporting Suggested stages: 1. load geometry 2. repair geometry 3. extract features 4. build size field 5. surface remesh 6. generate seeds 7. CVT / Voronoi 8. boundary clip 9. boundary layer 10. optimization 11. quality check 12. export # ALGORITHMIC EXPECTATIONS Use robust methods, not brittle heuristics. Recommended core approach: 1. Build a watertight, oriented, feature-aware surface mesh. 2. Build an AABB tree and signed distance field / inside-outside oracle. 3. Generate adaptive seeds using the size field. 4. Compute constrained CVT via Lloyd iterations. 5. Build Voronoi cells as half-space intersections. 6. Clip cells against the domain boundary. 7. Extract boundary faces from clipped cells. 8. Snap/project boundary entities to CAD/surface. 9. Merge coplanar faces and simplify small topological artifacts. 10. Optionally extrude boundary layers. 11. Optimize and validate topology/quality. 12. Export. If you choose a different robust approach, justify it and prove it with tests. # PROJECT STRUCTURE Create a clean repository layout: autopoly/ CMakeLists.txt README.md docs/ architecture.md parameters.md validation.md include/autopoly/ Types.h Geometry.h Feature.h SizeField.h SurfaceMesher.h VolumeMesher.h BoundaryLayer.h Quality.h Exporter.h Mesher.h Factory.h src/ Geometry.cpp Feature.cpp SizeField.cpp SurfaceMesher.cpp VolumeMesher.cpp BoundaryLayer.cpp Quality.cpp Exporter.cpp Mesher.cpp Factory.cpp cgal/ CgalKernel.h CgalKernel.cpp apps/ autopoly_cli.cpp python/ autopoly_pybind.cpp tests/ test_geometry.cpp test_surface_mesher.cpp test_volume_mesher.cpp test_quality.cpp test_export.cpp data/ cube.stl sphere.stl cylinder.stl broken_cube.stl thin_gap.stl sharp_feature.stl # TESTING REQUIREMENTS Add automated tests for